    <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6"><strong>Melissa in 2026:</strong> The town was platted in 1872 when the Houston and Texas Central Railroad came through, and an April 1921 tornado destroyed most of it — only a handful of buildings, including the old bank building on Cooper Street, survived. Population bottomed out around 285 in 1949 and stayed a small farm town for decades. It's a different place now: Melissa has grown from 14,339 residents in the 2020 Census to an estimated 32,900 in 2026, and most of that growth is new construction — meaning a lot of brand-new HVAC systems, and a lot of installers competing for the work.</p>
